      {
        "id": "n07_story",
        "type": "flograph.viz.story",
        "pos": [
          1700,
          400
        ],
        "label": "Two years at Northwind",
        "params": {
          "title": "Two years at Northwind",
          "subtitle": "The order the channels come in changed twice, and almost nobody noticed either one.",
          "steps": "# Two years, five channels\nEvery channel Northwind sells through started somewhere and ended\nsomewhere else. The slope draws the change itself, so the ones going the\nwrong way are the ones tilting down.\n\n---\n\n**Online nearly doubled** while the stores slid quietly for eight quarters\nrunning. Nothing here is a cliff \u2014 which is exactly why it took two years\nto notice.\n\n---\n\n@scene 2\n## The order changed twice\nRanking each quarter on its own turns the same numbers into a race, and an\novertake becomes a crossing you cannot miss.\n\nMarketplace passed the trade counter in 2024 Q4. Online passed the stores\none quarter later.\n\n---\n\nNobody left and nobody arrived. The whole story is five lines swapping\nplaces \u2014 which a chart of the revenue itself would have buried, because\nevery one of these lines is still growing or shrinking gently.\n\n---\n\n@scene 3\n## What the book looks like now\nA hundred squares, shared out by the last quarter alone. Online is most of\na third of it; the trade counter is now the rounding error the stores used\nto treat it as.\n",
          "prose_side": "left",
          "prose_width": 38,
          "transition": "fade",
          "progress": true,
          "width": 820,
          "height": 620
        }
      }
    ],
